From f676a4435d27405c00409edae1c34c8112fbac54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leo <leoschlosser@tutamail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:30:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 130/130] power: reset: reboot-mode: write the normal mode for
 commands without one

A reboot command that names no mode left the mode register as it was. On
midas S-Boot reads the mode from INFORM3, so a reboot into the recovery
stuck to every reboot after it: "Reboot system now" in the LineageOS
recovery (Android's "reboot,userrequested") or "adb reboot" went back
into the recovery. The midas reboot mode patch lists it as a TODO.

Write the normal mode, where the device tree has one, for any command
that matches no mode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c b/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
index 3611bed34..5b1d18fd1 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
@@ -109,6 +109,12 @@ static int reboot_mode_notify(struct notifier_block *this,
 
 	reboot = container_of(this, struct reboot_mode_driver, reboot_notifier);
 	magic = get_reboot_mode_magic(reboot, cmd);
+	/*
+	 * A command that names no mode ("userrequested", "shell", "") is a normal
+	 * reboot, not one that keeps the mode of the boot before.
+	 */
+	if (!magic && cmd)
+		magic = get_reboot_mode_magic(reboot, NULL);
 	if (magic)
 		reboot->write(reboot, magic);
 
